> 
> I'm not sure fast kills prevents monsters from quaffing gain level. 

IME it doesn't prevent those potions from being drunk; all intelligent
monsters that have such potions seem to quaff them instantly (or quite
instantly).

> It
> most likely does help to prevent them from quaffing healing potions or
> reading teleport scrolls. 

Yes, exactly. So building huge stacks is easier if you kill the critters
fast. Then only few potions of gain level or gain energy (and/or speed)
are necessary to alchemize those stacks. IME, being able to kill most of
those intelligent monsters with two hits (two-weaponing, or multi-fire
highly enchanted missile weapons) is sufficient to obtain larger stacks.

> It might help to prevent them from throwing
> offensive potions like blindness that I can later polypile in the hopes of
> making gain level.

Comparably large amounts of potions of gain level are generated in monster
inventory (where you usually don't get them from), but polypiles will
(AFAIK) be subject to the random object generation probabilities, so you
need many potions for polypiling for a chance to get the desired rare ones.
And, in the first place, you need some means to polypile of course, which
is not granted, since [wands of] polymorph is also not that common.

